<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21285" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭassus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭāsus</span></b> , i, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰασσός</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰᾶσός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an ancient and wealthy town on the coast of
			Caria</i>, now <i>Askem</i> or <i>Asyn
				Kalessi</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 29, 29, § 107</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">9, 8, 8, §
			27</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 32, 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">33, 30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">37,
			17</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭassĭus</span></b> 
			or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭāsĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Iassus</i>, <i>Iassian</i>: sinus. <i><span class="en">Mel. 1</span></i>, 
			 16 <i>fin.</i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 29,
				29, § 107</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭas-senses</span></b> ,
				ĭum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Iassus</i>, <i>Iassians</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Liv.
				37, 17</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
